B.a90=new A.fl("record","How do I record something?","The gold microphone button, from anywhere in the app. It starts a new song and goes straight into recording \u2014 no naming, no choosing where it lives. You can do both afterwards, once there is something worth filing.\n\nTo add a recording to a song you already have, open it and press Record on the toolbar.",B.aZg)
B.bbZ=s(["take","takes","another","add","overdub","layer","part","second","share","shared"],t.s)
B.a9c=new A.fl("take","How do I add a take to a song?","Open the song and press Record on the toolbar. That adds a new take alongside the ones already there.\n\nA take stays private to you until you share it. Press Takes to see all of them and share the one you want the room to hear \u2014 nothing you have not shared is ever audible to anybody, including on the Open Mic.",B.bbZ)
B.aYa=s(["chord","chords","sheet","lyrics","words","key","tempo","bpm","transcribe","transcription","tab","analyse","analyze","notation"],t.s)
B.a98=new A.fl("sheet","How do I get the chords and words for my song?","Record something first, then open the song and press Song Sheet.\n\nCoLabRoom listens to the recording, works out every chord, finds the key and the tempo, and writes down the words you sang \u2014 then puts the chords over the words. It takes a few minutes and it keeps going if you leave the screen.",B.aYa)
B.b_y=s(["who","hear","private","privacy","public","see","visible","audience","secret","safe","sharing","permission"],t.s)
B.a9a=new A.fl("audience","Who can hear my song?","Look at the bar under the toolbar when a song is open. It always says who can hear it, and tapping it shows the whole picture:\n\n\u2022 Only you \u2014 nobody else is in the room it lives in\n\u2022 Your room \u2014 everybody in that room\n\u2022 People you asked \u2014 somebody invited to this one song\n\u2022 Anyone \u2014 it is on the Open Mic\n\nYou can move it back down at any time, and a take you have not shared stays private no matter where the song sits.",B.b_y)
B.aqV=s(["open","mic","publish","post","share","public","everybody","stage","upload","showcase"],t.s)
B.a91=new A.fl("openmic","How do I put a song on the Open Mic?",'Open the song, tap the bar that says who can hear it, then "Put it on the Open Mic".\n\nAnybody signed in can then find it, listen, and offer to play on it. Only the takes your room has already heard become audible \u2014 never one you are still working on privately. The same bar takes it back down whenever you like.',B.aqV)
B.aXu=s(["take","off","remove","delete","down","unpublish","private","hide","undo","mic"],t.s)
B.a93=new A.fl("takedown","How do I take a song off the Open Mic?",'Open the song, tap the bar that says who can hear it, then "Take it off the Open Mic". It stops being findable immediately.\n\nNothing you did while it was up is lost \u2014 the song, the takes and the song sheet all stay exactly as they were.',B.aXu)
B.aT6=s(["ask","help","request","collaborate","collaborator","someone","somebody","musician","find","need","bass","drummer","singer"],t.s)
B.a9_=new A.fl("ask","How do I ask somebody for help on a song?","Two ways, depending on whether you have somebody in mind.\n\nIf you do: find them in the Open Mic, open their profile, and ask them. They see the one song you named and nothing else of yours until they say yes.\n\nIf you do not: put the song on the Open Mic and say what it needs. It then shows up for people who play that part, and they can offer.",B.aT6)
B.aY6=s(["asked","invite","invited","invitation","notification","bell","accept","decline","yes","request","join"],t.s)
B.a9e=new A.fl("answer-ask","Somebody asked me to play on their song. Where is it?","In your notifications \u2014 the bell in the top corner. Open it and you can say yes or no.\n\nSaying yes gives you that one song, not the rest of their work. Saying no tells them and nothing else happens.",B.aY6)
B.aWo=s(["room","rooms","band","group","folder","catalog","organise","organize","make","create","new"],t.s)
B.a9f=new A.fl("rooms","What is a room, and how do I make one?","A room is who can see a set of songs \u2014 your band, a side project, or just the songs you write on your own. Every song lives in one, and the room decides who hears it.\n\nMake one from Your music: press New song and create a room without leaving the flow, or open the rooms list and press New room.",B.aWo)
B.aXS=s(["invite","add","member","bandmate","friend","room","join","collaborator","people"],t.s)
B.a99=new A.fl("invite-room","How do I invite somebody to my room?","Open the room and press the person icon in the top corner.\n\nA room invitation is everything in it, now and later \u2014 so if you only want somebody on one song, ask them to play on that song instead. You can also invite somebody you met on the Open Mic straight from their profile.",B.aXS)
B.aX5=s(["remove","kick","member","leave","left","quit","band","delete","someone"],t.s)
B.a92=new A.fl("remove-member","How do I remove somebody from a room?","Open the room, then the members list, and remove them there. They lose the room and every song in it.\n\nWhat they already recorded stays \u2014 a take keeps its author, and removing somebody does not erase the work they did with you.",B.aX5)
B.aWG=s(["sounds","like","genre","style","taste","tags","profile","describe","match","matching"],t.s)
B.a9b=new A.fl("sounds-like",'What does "sounds like" do on my profile?','It is how the app finds people making the kind of music you make. "Guitarist" does not say whether you play metal or jazz; this does.\n\nNobody is ranked by it. It moves you sideways towards people in the same corner, never up or down past anybody. Set it from your profile, under the tuning icon. Five words at most \u2014 fewer and sharper works better than listing everything.',B.aWG)
B.aeK=s(["discoverable","found","find","visible","hidden","profile","appear","listed","city","location","search"],t.s)
B.a9g=new A.fl("discoverable","How do I show up in the Open Mic, or stop showing up?","Your profile, under the tuning icon in the corner. It is off until you turn it on \u2014 nobody appears in the Open Mic without choosing to.\n\nThe same place decides who can see your city: nobody, only people you have made something with, or anybody browsing.",B.aeK)
B.aXr=s(["set","sets","setlist","list","gig","order","practice","performance","live"],t.s)
B.a94=new A.fl("sets","How do I make a set list?","In Your music, switch from Songs to Sets and press New set.\n\nA set is a running order for one occasion \u2014 Friday practice, Saturday's show \u2014 built from songs you already have, in whatever order you will play them.",B.aXr)
B.b2z=s(["find","lost","missing","gone","where","cannot","disappeared","search","song","deleted"],t.s)
B.a96=new A.fl("missing-song","I cannot find a song I made.","Everything you have is in Your music, grouped by the room it lives in. If you cannot see it, use the search box \u2014 it matches titles, room names, and a lyric you remember.\n\nIf it was somebody else's song you were invited to, it is under their room rather than yours.",B.b2z)
B.b_j=s(["report","block","abuse","harassment","inappropriate","offensive","spam","copyright","stolen","complaint","flag"],t.s)
B.a9h=new A.fl("report","Somebody posted something they should not have.","Report it. There is a flag on a song's public page, on a person's profile under the More menu, and on a room under the same menu.\n\nYou can also block somebody from their profile \u2014 you stop seeing each other completely, in both directions, and they are not told.\n\nSomebody reads every report.",B.b_j)
B.b1a=s(["refund","money","pay","paid","payment","charge","charged","cost","price","subscription","billing","cancel","free","premium","upgrade"],t.s)
B.a95=new A.fl("refund","How do I get a refund? What does this cost?","Nothing. There is no paid tier and no way to pay for anything in CoLabRoom right now, so there is nothing to refund.\n\nIf you were charged by something calling itself CoLabRoom, it was not us \u2014 tell us at support@colabroom.com and do not pay it.",B.b1a)
B.aY2=s(["delete","account","remove","close","quit","leave","erase","data","gdpr","deactivate"],t.s)
B.a97=new A.fl("delete-account","How do I delete my account?","Your account screen, at the bottom. It removes your profile, your rooms and everything in them.\n\nIt cannot be undone, and takes with it songs other people may be working on with you \u2014 so if you share a room, hand it over first.",B.aY2)
B.aWV=s(["demo","fake","bot","test","real","account","label","chip","seeded","nobody"],t.s)
B.a9d=new A.fl("demo","What is a DEMO account?","A seeded account, not a person. They exist so the app can be tested with a crowd in it before there is a real one.\n\nThey are always labelled, they will never answer you, and asking one to play on your song will not go anywhere. They are removed in batches as real people arrive.",B.aWV)
